reported, proposed 4 times: source positions compared column by column regardless of line: Span.contained checks startCol<=other.startCol and endCol>=other.endCol even when the lines differ (Span(1:10..5:2) does not contain Span(2:1..3:50)); Token.makeSpan floors the end column of a one line last token at first.column() even when first is on an earlier line (a at 1:10 to x at 3:1 gives 1:10..3:10)
refused, proposed 6 times: columns counted in code points by the tokenizer (MetaTokenizer, Token.makeSpan) but used as UTF-16 char indexes by Message (nextVisible/prevVisible charAt(col-1), visualCol, visualDelta, tabAwareWidth, expandTabs): after a character outside the BMP the caret shrinks the wrong span and tabs expand to the wrong stop ("\uD83D\uDE00a b" span 1:2..1:4 underlines "a " only): unreachable, every source is checked against Fs.allowed first and tokenizing stops at the first character outside it (see ruledOut)
reported, proposed 1 time: Message splits the raw source on \R while MetaTokenizer drops a leading BOM and breaks lines only at \n: in a file starting with a BOM every error on line 1 shows a ? in front and the marker one column off; the illegal character error on a form feed shows the text before it as the whole line, with no caret
refused, proposed 2 times: tab widths in Message caret math measured from the wrong start column: visualCol counts tab stops from 1 while expandTabs draws them from 0, and visualDelta measures tabs inside a span as if the span began at column 0 ("a\tx" marks the space before x; "ab\txyz" span 1:2..1:4 gets one caret too many): unreachable for the same reason
reported, proposed 1 time: truncation counting the "..." ellipsis as one character: PrettyFileName.shorten keeps maxLen-1 characters and prepends "..." in its n<=2 and last resort branches, returning 82 characters for a limit of 80 (mem:aaa..100 chars gives "..." plus 79 a); PrettyToken.show keeps 21 plus "..." for 24, correctly; made moot: file names are no longer truncated (relative to the working directory or absolute, like compilers do)
refused, proposed 1 time: span ends off by one when the last token ends with a newline (Token.makeSpan clamps c-1=0 to column 1 of the next line; MetaTokenizer file span ends one past the last character): unreachable, the only Fearless tokens ending with a newline are white space and an unclosed block comment, whose errors render the same with or without it (see ruledOut)
refused, proposed 1 time: MetaParser back end operations (peekLast, expectLast, expectAnyLast, spanLast) do not check index<limit, so after the front consumed everything they return an already consumed token and leave limit<index: unreachable, the grammars only call expectLast for the closer of a group whose opener was just consumed (the token tree guarantees both) or before consuming from the front (see ruledOut)
refused, proposed 1 time: MetaParser spans of a token range computed from its two end tokens without skipping the skip tokens at the ends: span(low,high) is empty when an end token is white space, so remainingSpan/spanLast fall back to the whole parser span (including consumed tokens), and spanAround takes the wrong end of its boundary tokens: unreachable, the Fearless parser skips only _SOF/_EOF, which parseFileFull consumes before any span is taken; white space is removed by postTokenize (see ruledOut)
refused, proposed 1 time: Message assumes positions are inside the line text: a span one column past the end of a line gets no caret (makeCaretLine), ensureContainment runs before trimInvisible so the outer span may stop containing the inner one, and renderMulti repeats lines when the caret is outside the frame: unreachable, Frontend end of file and missing closer errors point at a real token (see ruledOut)
reported, proposed 1 time: TreeDiagnostics.tryRemove counts a recovery parse that fails on the final _EOF as a full success (ofRecovery returns nextIndex, equal to ts.size() both on success and on failing at _EOF), so removing the closer "fixes" a missing closer and the error blames it: "A:{ .m:A -> this.foo( }" says This "}" may be unintended, while removing the "(" is what makes the file parse
refused, proposed 1 time: MetaTokenizer.whiteList counts positions from 1:1 instead of the startingPosition fields, so illegal character errors in a fragment tokenized from 3:5 land at 1:3: unreachable, Parse.from is the only tokenizer and starts at 1:1 (see ruledOut)
reported, proposed 6 times: paths written into a text format that splits and interprets them, without that format's quoting: LinuxAssociations.desktopEntry writes Exec=<command> %f raw (a launcher under "/opt/my apps/" runs /opt/my), JavacTool.argToken quotes only for whitespace and " while javac argument files also treat ' as a quote and # as a comment (a source under it's/src is read as its/src); the XML escaping of the identity in the MIME package, proposed with it, is unreachable: the identity is the launcher file name set by the build
